{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"text":" gives each destination its batches in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order the events were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns. Batches that arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its oldest batch when full, so a destination that falls behind doesn’t hold up the others.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The delivery reports each batch dropped. Once the destination has caught up, it gets the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dropped batch’s records that a store keeps, read back from the store, after the newer batches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it received meanwhile; those kept in memory only are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is what tells the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have reached it in an earlier run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference"},{"text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinat